---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const updated = '2026-11-15';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The terms that apply to using SoloYolo's free business calculators and document tools."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Terms of use' }]} />

    <article class="max-w-3xl pt-8 pb-16 sm:pt-12">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-[clamp(2.1rem,1.4rem+3.4vw,3.4rem)] font-medium leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.03em]">
        Terms of use
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: <time datetime={updated}>{updated}</time></p>

      <div class="prose-ledger mt-10">
        <p>
          By using SoloYolo ("the site") you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do
          not use the site.
        </p>

        <h2>What the site is</h2>
        <p>
          SoloYolo provides free, browser-based business calculators and document tools for
          freelancers and small service businesses. Everything the tools produce (rates, margins,
          figures, generated documents) is <strong>informational output only</strong>. It is not
          tax, accounting, legal or financial advice, and it is not a substitute for a qualified
          professional who knows your situation. Country-specific behaviour is documented with its
          official source; you remain responsible for checking your own obligations with your tax
          authority or adviser.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The site and its tools are provided "as is" and "as available". Formulas are tested, but
          no warranty is given that results are complete, accurate or fit for your particular
          purpose, or that the service will be uninterrupted or error-free. You use the tools and
          act on their results at your own risk.
        </p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Do not attempt to disrupt, overload or reverse-engineer the site's infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Do not present the site's output as your own professional advice to third parties.</li>
          <li>Do not use automated means to interact with advertising or artificially inflate ad impressions or clicks.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Your content</h2>
        <p>
          The tools process everything you type locally in your browser. You keep all rights to
          your data; we never receive it. Documents you generate are yours to use.
        </p>

        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The site's name, design, code and written content are the property of the site's
          operator. You may quote short excerpts with attribution and a link; wholesale copying of
          pages or code is not permitted.
        </p>

        <h2>Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          The site is funded by advertising served through Google AdSense for visitors who consent
          to ads. Advertising never changes how a tool calculates. See the
          <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for how ad cookies work and how to turn ads off.
        </p>

        <h2>Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, the site's operator is not liable for any loss
          arising from use of the site or reliance on its output, including lost profit, lost
          business or mispriced work.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          These terms may change as the toolkit grows; the "last updated" date above always shows
          the current version. Questions about these terms can go to
          <a href="mailto:hello@soloyolo.example">hello@soloyolo.example</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
